# mcp-server-geo-optimizer

Cursor agent rules for this repository. Follow these constraints on every change.

## Scope

- Work only inside this repository. Never modify sibling projects.
- One layer at a time: domain → infrastructure → services → tools → server.

## Architecture

- Transport and MCP protocol stay in `src/index.ts` and `src/server.ts`.
- Tools define schemas and thin handlers only. Keep handlers under 30 lines.
- Services contain business logic and must never import `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk`.
- Domain functions are pure: no HTTP, no I/O, no MCP types.
- External clients are injected. Do not import HTTP clients into domain code.

## TypeScript

- Strict mode: `noImplicitAny`, `strictNullChecks`, `exactOptionalPropertyTypes`.
- Every exported function must have an explicit return type.
- Never use `any`. Use `unknown` with type guards.
- Prefer `readonly` arrays and interfaces for immutable data.
- Keep functions under 40 lines. Extract helpers early.
- One tool per file in `src/tools/`. Export only the tool definition object.

## Errors

- Throw `McpError` from `src/utils/errors.ts` at the service/tool boundary.
- Domain code throws `DomainError` only.
- Codes: `InvalidParams`, `InternalError`, `GeocodingFailed`, `ROUTE_FAIL`, `CLUSTER_FAIL`, `GEOMETRY_FAIL`, `PROVIDER_CONFIG`, `TIMEOUT`, `UPSTREAM_ERROR`.
- Preserve existing `McpError` codes when wrapping (`wrapError`); never re-label a `TIMEOUT` as a generic failure.
- Redact secrets (`redactUrl` / `redactSecrets`) in every error message and log line. Do not rely on production masking.
- Never leak stack traces to MCP clients in production. Log them on stderr.
- Validate all tool inputs with Zod. Fail fast.

## Testing

- Every file in `src/domain/` has a matching test in `tests/unit/domain/`.
- Every tool has at least one integration test.
- Use deterministic seeds for clustering tests.
- Mock all HTTP. Never hit real APIs in tests.
- Maintain at least 80% statement, branch, function, and line coverage across `src/` (excluding `src/index.ts`).

## Logging

- stdout is reserved for MCP stdio. All logs go to stderr as JSON.

## Commits

- Branches: `feature/<kebab-name>`, `fix/<kebab-name>`, `refactor/<kebab-name>`.
- Commits: Conventional Commits, e.g. `feat(tools): add time-window support to optimizeRoute`.
